    feat(m2): digest the bytes the pilot already read, for canary integrity
    
    M2 Slice 3B3 needs to prove the files a canary cites are the files it expected,
    and the one-time budget forbids reading them again to check. The pilot dropped
    the text it had read, so no digest was reachable from outside and the only
    alternatives were a second read (against the budget, and bypassing the reader's
    descriptor checks) or hashing nothing.
    
    Each file summary now carries a SHA-256 of the text this invocation obtained,
    computed from the same string the evidence core produced. No extra open, no
    extra bytes, no weakened check. The digest is over decoded UTF-8, which
    re-encodes byte-identically except for a leading BOM that TextDecoder strips;
    that caveat is recorded on the type so a BOM-prefixed file fails closed rather
    than silently matching.
    
    Additive: no existing field changed and no existing test altered.

